{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1007021-dracula-the-visionary-and-the-purpose-of-the-ordo-dracul","id":1007021,"title":"Dracula the visionary and the purpose of the Ordo Dracul...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-22T21:23:22-08:00","id":1007021,"title":"Dracula the visionary and the purpose of the Ordo Dracul...","content":"I've been thinking about Dracula lately and a here's a thought that came across my mind....<br /> <br /> What if Dracula is a &quot;Andrew Ryan&quot; style visionary who wishes to build a &quot;Vampire Utopian Society&quot; that resembles &quot;Annio Dracula&quot; to &quot;Vampire Hunter D&quot; especially the latter and maybe this is perhaps the Ordo Dracul's true purpose is to move forward this &quot;visionary utopia&quot; of his?<br /> <br /> Or basically try to think about the Nobility from Vampire Hunter D or basically Castlevania but more supernatural/mythical based instead of super science of the former which plays into the same idea that Vampires are masters of the world and everyone of them are like &quot;Counts&quot;/Countesses&quot; which they have their own castles which humans live in villages which act like herds for vampires to feed upon and depending how they rule it. Basically Dracula's world vision of a &quot;Vampire Utopia&quot; that each Vampire get to be their own &quot;Vlord/Ladies of the Night&quot;.<br /> <br /> Oh another thing too about the Ordo Dracul's structure that there could be a structure similar to Warhammer's Vampires since for example there's the Von Carnstein and the Blood Dragons which the former is the actual Nobility that harkens back to the classic Dracula image of the Vampire in their castles in the Carpathian mountains while the Blood Dragons are the warriors/mercenaries of the Ordo Dracul that serve the Nobility's cause which also harkens back to Dracula's days as a warrior knight. Of course all of this is just brainstorming ideas in my head about things.<br /> <br /> So any ideas?<br /> <br /> Well to put it planely, imagine if you're playing a normal game of Reqiuem in modern nights but you've fallen into Torpor and your characters wake up and find themselves in a Far Future that looks very similar to Vampire Hunter D during the Nobility's heyday (well the major inspiration of this plot came from Wolfenstein: The New Order's plotline) and they'll be like &quot;Wait..what the hell happened?&quot; even more interesingly anough, what if the player characters were in the Carthians and some of them were in the Ordo Dracul and what the latter has a faction Civil War between the Dragons who basically want to keep society as it is vs the &quot;Utopians&quot; and the characters have fallen into Torpor during this civil war and they've waken up like a hundred or thousand years later which now Vampires rule the earth under the leadership and guidance or rather the world has been remade into Dracula's vision and he's like the &quot;Andrew Ryan/Comstock&quot; expy character.<br /> <br /> Well the reason I'm writing this idea, it's actually fun to explore the conflict of Vampires who wish to keep the Masquerade and hide in the shadows while allowing humans direct their future vs Vampires who want to rule humans openly due to the belief that humans are not only inferior but also they have the inability to rule themselves and they need superior beings like them to guide their future &quot;for their own good&quot;.<br /> <br /> Basically the main plot of the once the PCs raise from Torpor, they're like a relic from a bygone era and completely out of place since they still be wearing their modern era clothes (leather jackets, jeans etc) which the Vampires of this era resemble well Nobles like the ladies wear elegant elaborate ballgowns while the lords well looks like a Dracula copy while the Blood Dragon knights wear red armor that resemble Francis Cord Coppla's Dracula armor from the beginning and how they look in Warhammer not to mention they command a bunch of monsters which feels like Castlevania. I think the main goal might fight through this world, kill Dracula and try to find a way to travel back to the past to avert this from happening like the very moment before they went to torpor and prevented that from happening therefore able to finish a task that could have prevented that future from happening at all.<br /> <br /> In short: WoD Requiem meets Warhammer Vampire Counts, Caslevania and Vampire Hunter D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-23-2016, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T06:43:44-08:00","id":1007206,"title":"","content":"This seems like a wonderful <i>World of Darkness: Mirrors</i> settings, and I strongly recommend checking out the God Machine Chronicle at the back of the <i>Chronicles of Darkness </i>book, especially the Time and Space track if you want to include the time travel portion.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Ordo Dracul Utopia is a variant timeline which is used as Logistic Infrastructure to mass produce an output of certain types of Angels, which then follow the PCs back to the main timeline where the PCs prevent the Utopia. The God-Machine can then use the Angels from the alternate future timeline to create Infrastructure in the main timeline. The fact these Angels are produced in a timeline that no one but the PCs experience is powerful Concealment Infrastructure, but that leaves one to wonder about the Elimination Infrastructure after the PCs change the past to prevent the timeline. Its a bit like a self-cleaning oven in its horrible perfection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-23-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:29:57-08:00","id":1008333,"title":"","content":"Perhaps another thing too, what about somehow importing Castelvania itself into Requiem which first serves as some mythical castle similar to how the Sierra Madre was in Fallout New Vegas, even though we know that <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bran_Castle\" target=\"_blank\">Bran Castle</a> exists but what if that entire castle could serve as a &quot;Lighthouse&quot; equivalent (to the Bioshock series) to the actual &quot;Castlevania&quot; that points to the moon if you face the right direction in some ritual or something (I think it's hard to explain but it involves any area that Dracula or Vlad Tepes once had his &quot;mark of history&quot; that is in order to find him...) that is actually located in CoD's version of the Umbra (whatever it's called) which is also where his base of operations would be located if he ever enacted his &quot;Vampire Hunter D Nobility&quot; utopia since we all know that it's currently unknown about Dracula's whereabouts are.<br /> <br /> Anyways point is, I thought it would be cool that Vlad Tepes's current whereabouts that he's actually somewhere in the Shadow Realms or anywhere in the Chronicles of Darkness cosmology where his &quot;Castlevania&quot; can be located not to mention it's also always night time as well and sometimes the castle can materialize into our world at times and out. I think this idea was played into even Nosferatu where the villagers mention a &quot;Phantom Castle&quot; that sometimes cannot be found during the daylight if I'm remembering this correctly.<br /> <br /> I guess all of this could be why Dracula himself would be extremely difficult to find or his grande mythical castle that is actually alive and constantly changing as far I know of Castlevania lore.<br /> <br /> Or maybe porting the WoD cosmology like the Umbra or a Horizon Realm might be much easier though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:57:21-08:00","id":1008347,"title":"","content":"The CofD equivalent of the middle umbra is called the <i>hisil</i>, or shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}